          "kind": "prose",
          "body": "An OCaml project is a directory with one file at the top of it that says what the project is. Dune reads that file, reads the dune file in every directory below it, and works out what to build. The compiler never sees the project as a whole: it compiles one module at a time and hands the pieces to the linker."
